A||||7||2birds||Anybody from Memphis, TN area?||||1||
Z||000000||2birds||10-27-2001||09:16 PM||||I might be transferring to the Memphis, TN area soon.  Any input on the area would be appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||10-28-2001||01:07 AM||||Lived there in the past. Traffic, heat, ice storms, usual big city crime. BUT, Memphis in May is great. Job market was good then and<BR>reasonable housing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fogglethorpe||10-28-2001||02:28 PM||||One reason not to go: Al Gore.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WampusCat||10-28-2001||06:22 PM||||Hey, AlGore is from the other side of the state!  My7Fieros is a cop near here so he can tell you all about the dregs of society.  I've been here 2.5 years and it's not too bad.  There's plenty of good food and blues.  If you have kids, you don't want them going to school in the City of Memphis.  Worst academic performance in the state with the highest budget.  The 'burbs aren't bad for schools.  <BR>  If you don't have kids, I recommend Midtown or downtown for the nightlife/resturants. <BR>  My main gripes are:  1-It's freakin' humid and hot here in the summer.  I used to live in the very southwest corner of AZ, and that's downright comfortable in the summer compared to here.  2-It's flat as a pancake for 100 miles around.  No twisty roads, no hills to hike in...flat.  3-Most people here don't know how to drive a car.  Traffic is ridiculous here.  Not the volume, just the general widespread incompetence...worse than anywhere else I have lived.  <BR>  Hope this doesn't sound too negative...notice I haven't moved away.  It's cheap to live here and prople are generally friendly.  Any specific questions, let me know.<P>Steve||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||10-28-2001||09:38 PM||||Well I guess I'll come out of my shell for a minute...I havent posted anything on here in quite a while, it was starting to get rediculas on here w/ all the newbies.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>Anyway yes I live here to. Its ok, there's worse places to live. What kind of work do you do? Unless you want to get robbed on a daily basis, you need to move to the east end of town. Any of the 'burbs are fine to. Germantown, Bartlett, Cordova, Collierville, ect. Theres alot of potential w/ this city. If the bad element wasnt here, it'd be great (like any other city I guess.) Oh well, if you move here, lemme know!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My7logo_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||2birds||10-29-2001||10:07 PM||||I'm in the running for a job at the Bureau of Naval Personnel, at the old Millington NAS.  Being a submariner, it's one of the few Navy towns I've never been to.  I'm pretty happy living in SE Georgia right now, but shore duty is coming up quick.  I noticed there is an NHRA track on the NW side, and I figure I'll have to make a pilgrimage to Beale Street someday.  It's a bit closer to my real home (Iowa) anyway.  I figure I'll probably look mainly on the North side, but I'm just curious what the area is like.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||WampusCat||10-29-2001||10:51 PM||||The north side of Memphis is a high crime area.  If you mean north of Memphis, out closer to Millington, then you're OK as far as crime.  Here's a link to a map that rates areas on likelihood of murder, robbery, or rape.  I can't vouch for it's accuracy but the impression that I've gotten from driving in those neighborhoods pretty much agrees with the map.  I live in Midtown near Overton Square (all 1's and 2's on the map).  <A HREF="http://www.apbnews.com/resourcecenter/datacenter/crimecheck/mallcrime/mallmap2.asp?id=34840" TARGET=_blank>http://www.apbnews.com/resourcecenter/datacenter/crimecheck/mallcrime/mallmap2.asp?id=34840</A> <p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||2birds||10-30-2001||01:38 AM||||Nice town...<BR>By North side, I suppose I mean Millington and points North of there.<BR>Thanks for the map.<BR>||||reg||1
